# Settings for sending from a passkey account (a phone with no wallet app). All are read when the app is built, and
# everything below ends up in the page every visitor downloads: put NO key or secret in any of them. If the bundler or
# the sponsor needs a key, give the URL of a small proxy that holds it.
#
# With any of the first four missing, the app says "Backing from this phone is not switched on for this server yet" and
# the browser-wallet path is unchanged. With VITE_CREATON_PASSKEY_ACCOUNT unset or not 1, this feature is off entirely.

# Turn passkey sending on.
VITE_CREATON_PASSKEY_ACCOUNT=1
# The network the project lives on (also used for the Launcher below).
VITE_CREATON_CHAIN_ID=
# A node's address on that network, for reads and for the account's address.
VITE_CREATON_RPC_URL=
# Where a signed step is sent (an ERC-4337 bundler for EntryPoint 0.7).
VITE_CREATON_BUNDLER_URL=
# Where the network fee is asked to be paid. Optional: the bundler's address when unset. When set, the fee request goes ONLY
# here, never to the bundler, so put the per-account daily limit and the allow-list of target contracts in front of this
# address. An address with a name, a password or a key in its query is refused (the app then says it is not switched on).
# A refusal reaches the person in plain words ("the free network fee was refused ...") only when the sponsor's refusal
# text contains one of: polic, denied, forbid, unauthor, not allowed, exceed, quota. Any other wording reads as "did not go
# through"; word the daily-limit refusal with one of them (for example "daily limit exceeded").
#
# The server has that limit built in: `POST /sponsor` on the relay, in front of the operator's own sponsor (docs/web-push-deployment.md,
# section 2). Point this at `https://<the server>/sponsor`; it carries no key. The relay reads the operator's real sponsor
# address and the limits from its own environment (never from this file, never from a build): BUZZ_SPONSOR_UPSTREAM_URL,
# BUZZ_SPONSOR_PER_ACCOUNT_PER_DAY (default 10), BUZZ_SPONSOR_TOTAL_PER_DAY (default 1000), BUZZ_SPONSOR_PER_IP_PER_DAY
# (default 40), BUZZ_SPONSOR_EXIT_PER_IP_PER_DAY (default 200). Taking money out (leave, leaveTeam) is never refused by the
# per-account or server limit; its refusals say "daily limit exceeded" or "not allowed", words the list above holds.
VITE_CREATON_SPONSOR_URL=

# The earlier backers' claim page (step 4). All three, or the page does not exist: without them the address /earlier-grant is a plain
# "not found" and none of its code is loaded. Everything here ends up in the page every visitor downloads: an address, a fingerprint and a
# link, never a row of the list and never a key. The deployment must have been made with the earlier-grant settings
# (docs/next-version/DEPLOY-TEST-NETWORK.md); this build only points at it.
# The claim contract (the "earlier grants" address the deploy script prints and writes to its deployments file).
VITE_CREATON_EARLIER_CONTRACT=
# The fingerprint of the text a claimant accepts: the same value the deploy was given as EARLIER_TEXT_HASH.
VITE_CREATON_EARLIER_TEXT_HASH=
# Where a person can read that text (an http or https address with no name or password in it).
VITE_CREATON_EARLIER_TEXT_URL=
